<Base title="Privacy policy" description="How PHP Hub handles personal data.">
<div class="page-prose"><h1>Privacy policy</h1>
<p><em>Last updated: 8 November 2026.</em></p>
<p class="notice">This policy is a plain-language summary of current practice. It has not been reviewed by a lawyer and is not a verified legal statement.</p>
<!-- TODO(Raghav): add a contact email for privacy requests and review this text before relying on it legally. -->
<h2>What we collect</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Browsing:</strong> this site sets no cookies and uses no advertising trackers. We use cookieless Vercel Web Analytics for anonymous page-view statistics (see Analytics below). Search runs entirely in your browser.</li>
<li><strong>Hosting logs:</strong> our host (Vercel) may process technical data such as IP address and user agent to serve and secure the site.</li>
<li><strong>Contact form:</strong> if you send a request, we receive your name, email, site URL and message. The contact form is processed by <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener">Formspree</a>, a third-party form service, which receives and forwards your submission to us. A hidden anti-spam field is included; it collects nothing from genuine users.</li>
<li><strong>Newsletter:</strong> if you subscribe, your email address is stored by our email provider, Buttondown, to send briefs.</li></ul>
<h2>Data stored in your browser</h2>
<p>If you use the theme switch, bookmarks, reading history, or learning-path checkmarks, that choice is stored in localStorage on your device. PHP Hub does not receive it. Developer tools also run in the browser. Text you paste into a tool is not uploaded. You can clear bookmarks and history on the <a href="/saved">saved reading</a> page, or clear site data in your browser.</p>
<h2>Analytics</h2><p>We use <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy" rel="noopener">Vercel Web Analytics</a>, a privacy-friendly analytics service from our host. It sets no cookies and records anonymous, aggregated page views only. For each page view it may record the page URL, referrer, approximate location (country, region, city), browser, operating system and device type. Visitors are counted with a hash of the incoming request rather than a cookie, and that session data is discarded after 24 hours. We do not use it to identify you or follow you across other websites.</p>
<h2>How we use it</h2><p>Only to reply to your request, deliver work you asked for, or send the newsletter you signed up for. We do not sell personal data.</p>
<h2>Retention and your rights</h2><p>You can ask us to access, correct or delete your data at any time via the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. Newsletter emails include an unsubscribe link.</p>
<h2>Changes</h2><p>We will update this page if anything changes, for example if we add or change an analytics provider.</p></div></Base>
